    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0020033 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0020033">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009008"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sheath-like plant organ (PO:0009008) that surrounds the plumule (PO:0020032) of a plant embryo (PO:0009009) or the emerging shoot apex (PO:0000037) of a seedling.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PO_GIT:294</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cole&amp;#243ptile (Spanish, exact)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>子葉鞘、鞘葉 (Japanese, exact)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>plant_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>PO:0020033</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>The coleoptile is an outgrowth or part of the scutellum (PO:0020110) (which is a modified, haustorial cotyledon (PO:0020030)).  Develops separate from the shoot apical meristem (PO:0020148).  Found in Poaceae and other monocotyledons such as Zingiberaceae. Protects the emerging shoot system (PO:0009006) as it grows through the soil.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>coleoptile</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
