        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/po#TraitNet"/>
        <rdfs:comment>In bryophytes, particularly in mosses, a sporangium is referred to as a capsule. In seed plants, a sporangium is located in a sporophyll. In pteridophytes, a sporangium is located on the surface of a sporophyll or fertile leaf or borne on a sporangiophore. May be unicellular in some algae.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>sporangium</rdfs:label>
