        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>scab</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>plant_stress_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:comment>Symptoms and signs: one or more spikes or entire heads become bleached, superficial, often pink or organge masses of macrocondinia may be seen on and especially in the base of diseased spikelets. Small dark (blue black) perithesia will often be evident  sometimes after the ntial infection and especially abandant on on infected spikelets, notes, and crowns.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>wheat fusarium head blight fungal disease</rdfs:label>
